      "rev_n_21_4fee98_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_21_4fee98_0",
        "node_id": "n_21_4fee98",
        "thought_text": "Consider the problem as a set cover or matching problem where we need to assign Chosen Ones to unique new schools. However, since each new school only contains one student (the Chosen One), the cost is simply 1 per student who isn't already winning. The constraint 'can't use each made-up name more than once' implies we need distinct new schools for each moved student, but since we just need the count, the simple count of non-winning Chosen Ones remains the optimal solution.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-6620676422275731672",
